>><</lanLink>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Lake Return []
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to 'lake'>><<effects>><<lakeeffects>>
<<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.assistant>>
  <<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<</if>>
<<set $_historyKylarCompromised to
  $VanillaPlus.historyProject.kylar is 'sabotage' and
  $VanillaPlus.historyProject.kylarStreet and
  !$VanillaPlus.historyProject.kylarPrepared
>>
<<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.ruin to
  $VanillaPlus.historyProject.recovery is 'recorded' and !$_historyKylarCompromised ? 2 : 1
>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Back on the shore, you seal the golden statuette inside its padded pouch
    and lay the wet slates out beneath the trees.
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.recovery is 'recorded' and !$_historyKylarCompromised>>
      Your position sketch,
      measurements and recovery notes remain legible.
      <span class="green">The golden priestess statuette has a documented context.</span>
    <<elseif $_historyKylarCompromised>>
      Robin corrected the altered route,
      but the detour disturbed the entrance before you could record it.
      <span class="teal">The statuette is genuine, though part of its context has been lost.</span>
    <<else>>
      The statuette survived, but the disturbed silt makes its original position difficult to prove.
      <span class="teal">The recovery record remains incomplete.</span>
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.assistant>>
      Robin copies the fading measurements onto dry paper while you redraw the chamber.
        When <<person1>><<his>> hand begins to shake, <<he>> presses it against yours until both are steady.
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    回到湖岸后，你把金制女祭司像封进内衬软垫的回收袋，
    又将湿透的记录板摊在树下。
    <<if
      $VanillaPlus.historyProject.recovery is 'recorded' and
      !$_historyKylarCompromised
    >>你的位置草图、测量数据
      和回收记录仍然清晰可辨。
      <span class="green">金制女祭司像拥有完整记录的出土环境。</span>
    <<elseif $_historyKylarCompromised>>
      罗宾修正了被篡改的路线，
      绕路却在记录前搅乱了入口处的淤泥。
      <span class="teal">女祭司像本身确为真品，部分出土环境却已经丢失。</span>
    <<else>>
      女祭司像完好无损，但被搅动的淤泥使原本位置难以证实。
      <span class="teal">这份回收记录仍不完整。</span>
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.assistant>>
      你重画石室时，罗宾趁测量数据消退前，把它们誊写到干纸上。
        <<person1>><<his>>手指开始发抖时，<<he>>把手压在你的手上，直到两人都稳定下来。
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<lakeicon>><<link `lanSwitch('Return to the lake shore', '返回湖岸')` 'Lake Shore'>>
  <<endevent>>
<</link>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft []
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to 'home'>><<effects>>
<<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.assistant>>
  <<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<</if>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      You arrange the raid records,
      early catalogue cards and paint observations across the floor.
      The town's bombing is well documented. The painting's shifting colours are visible.
      Neither proves that its unknown artist predicted the red moons that followed.
    <<else>>
      You arrange the old catalogue cards, translations of the frame inscription
      and the painting's condition record across the floor.
      The object is centuries old. The tale attached to it changes from one telling to the next.
      Nothing you found turns one of those versions into an eyewitness account.
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.assistant>>
      Robin trims labels and pins them beside each piece of evidence.
        "This one says what the record shows," <<he>> says, passing you a card.
        "This one says what people believe. They shouldn't look the same."
    <<else>>
      Once each written claim is placed beside the physical evidence,
        the limit of your conclusion becomes as clear as the conclusion itself.
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      <br><br>
      Your forest-lake sketches and the statuette's recovery record sit in a separate folder.
      They make a striking fieldwork sidebar, but they do not supply a missing chapter in the painting's history.
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      你把空袭记录、早期目录卡
      和颜料观察笔记铺满地板。
      城镇遭受轰炸一事有充分记录，画作变幻的颜色也肉眼可见。
      两者都不能证明，无名画家曾预言后来出现的红月。
    <<else>>
      你把旧目录卡、画框题名译文和画作状况记录铺满地板。
      实物确有数百年历史，附着其上的故事却在每次讲述中变化。
      你找到的东西中，没有一样能把某个版本变成亲历记录。
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.assistant>>
      罗宾裁好标签，把它们钉在每份证据旁。
        “这张写记录能证明什么，”<<he>>说道，把一张卡递给你，
        “那张写人们相信什么。它们不该看起来完全一样。”
    <<else>>
      当每项书面说法都与实物证据并排放置后，
        你能够得出的结论，以及这条结论的界限，都变得同样清晰。
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      <br><br>
      森林湖草图和女祭司像的回收记录被你放进另一只文件夹。
      它们可以组成醒目的实地调查侧栏，却无法填补画作历史中缺失的一章。
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<historyicon>><<link
  `lanSwitch('Mark where the evidence ends', '明确标出证据的边界')`
  'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft Finish'
>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>><<ghistory>><br>
<<historyicon>><<link
  `lanSwitch('Present the best story as the missing truth', '把最动听的故事当成缺失的真相')`
  'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft Finish'
>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft Finish []
<<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.draft to $phase is 0 ? 25 : 12>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $phase is 0>>
      <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
        Your first panels reconstruct
        the documented raid and the painting's route back to the museum.
        The last separates its unusual pigment from the prediction later attached to it.
      <<else>>
        Your first panels establish the painting's age, title and damage.
        The last traces how incompatible versions gathered around the same image.
      <</if>>
      <span class="green">Your exhibition is ready.</span>
    <<else>>
      You join the gaps with the most dramatic version available.
      The display flows cleanly, so long as nobody asks which labels describe records
      and which describe your preferred story.
      <span class="teal">Your exhibition is ready.</span><<famesocial 1>>
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $phase is 0>>
      <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
        前几块展板复原有记录的空袭，
        以及画作辗转回到博物馆的经历。最后一块则把异常颜料与后来附会的预言分开。
      <<else>>
        前几块展板说明画作的年代、题名与损伤，
        最后一块则追踪彼此冲突的故事如何逐渐汇聚到同一幅画上。
      <</if>>
      <span class="green">你的展览已经准备完成。</span>
    <<else>>
      你用最富戏剧性的版本填平了所有空缺。
      整场展览显得十分流畅，前提是没人追问哪些标签来自记录，
      哪些只是你最中意的故事。
      <span class="teal">你的展览已经准备完成。</span><<famesocial 1>>
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br><<homeicon>><<link `lanSwitch('Put the project away', '收好项目')` 'Bedroom'>><</link>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Exhibition []
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to 'museum'>><<effects>><<npc Winter>><<person1>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Your display occupies one wall of the museum.
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      The red-moon painting hangs above
      a timeline of the raid, its return to the collection and the claims later attached to it.
    <<else>>
      The snake-woman painting hangs above its translated title,
      condition record and a branching map of the tale's incompatible versions.
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      A smaller case to one side contains
      the golden priestess statuette, your position sketch and a plainly labelled field note.
    <</if>>
  <br><br>
  Winter waits until the room quiets.
    "One question," <<he>> says.
    "What can this exhibition establish, and what must it leave unresolved?"
  <<option 'CN'>>
    你的展览占据了博物馆的一整面墙。
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      红月画作悬在展板上方，
      下方的时间线依次列出空袭、画作回归藏品，以及后来附着其上的种种说法。
    <<else>>
      蛇女画作悬在展板上方，下面依次展示题名译文、状况记录，
      以及一张向外分岔的图表，梳理彼此冲突的故事版本。
    <</if>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      侧边另有一只较小的展柜，
      放着金制女祭司像、位置草图，以及明确标注为实地记录的说明。
    <</if>>
  <br><br>
  温特等房间安静下来。“最后一个问题。”<<he>>说道，
    “这场展览能够确认什么，又必须把什么留作未知？”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<set $_historyCorrectAnswer to
  $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'
    ? lanSwitch(
      'The records establish the raid and the painting, not a prediction',
      '记录可以确认空袭与画作，却不能证明预言'
    )
    : lanSwitch(
      'The object establishes an old painting and a changing tale, not the event depicted',
      '实物可以确认古老画作与变化的传说，却不能证明画中事件'
    )
>>
<<historyicon>><<link
  $_historyCorrectAnswer
  'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result'
>>
  <<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.final to 15>>
  <<if
    $VanillaPlus.historyProject.archive +
      $VanillaPlus.historyProject.museum +
      $VanillaPlus.historyProject.draft +
      $VanillaPlus.historyProject.final is 100
  >>
    <<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.status to 'won'>>
  <<else>>
    <<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.status to 'done'>>
  <</if>>
<</link>><<ghistory>><br>
<<museumicon>><<link
  `lanSwitch(
    'The painting is old, so its story must be true',
    '画作年代久远，所以其中的故事必定真实'
  )`
  'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result'
>>
  <<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.final to 0>>
  <<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.status to 'done'>>
<</link>><br>
<<historyicon>><<link
  `lanSwitch('The most repeated version is the original account', '流传最广的版本就是最初记录')`
  'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result'
>>
  <<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.final to 0>>
  <<set $VanillaPlus.historyProject.status to 'done'>>
<</link>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result []
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to 'museum'>><<effects>><<npc Winter>><<person1>>
<<set $_historyScore to
  $VanillaPlus.historyProject.archive +
    $VanillaPlus.historyProject.museum +
    $VanillaPlus.historyProject.draft +
    $VanillaPlus.historyProject.final
>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.status is 'won'>>
      "Exactly," Winter says.
        <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
          "The raid belongs to the town's history. The painting's strange behaviour belongs to the object.
          Its supposed foresight remains an interpretation."
        <<else>>
          "The frame, canvas and records establish an old painting with an old reputation.
          They do not turn its subject into a witness."
        <</if>>
      <br><br>
      <<He>> turns to the visitors.
        "This conclusion stands precisely because the exhibit does not claim more than its evidence."
        The questions that follow are directed to you rather than Winter.
        You answer each one without needing to look at your notes.
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 75>>
      Winter studies your display before nodding.
        "Good work. Your conclusion is sound, though parts of the chain rely too heavily on assumption."
        The visitors remain to examine your reconstruction.
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 50>>
      "You found a plausible story," Winter says.
        "Next time, prove it before you present it as fact."
        <<He>> leaves your display open for the afternoon.
    <<else>>
      Winter corrects several labels while the visitors move on.
        "Research is not decoration," <<he>> says quietly.
        "You need evidence before confidence."
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.status is 'won'>>
      “完全正确。”温特说道，
        <<if $VanillaPlus.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
          “空袭属于城镇的历史，画作的异常变化属于实物本身。
          至于它是否曾预示未来，仍然只是一种解释。”
        <<else>>
          “画框、画布与记录可以确认，这是一幅声名流传已久的古老画作。
          它们却不能让画中人物变成历史见证者。”
        <</if>>
      <br><br>
      <<He>>转向参观者。
        “这个结论之所以站得住，正是因为这场展览没有声称证据之外的事。”
        接下来的问题全都抛向你，而非温特。你不必查看笔记，便逐一作出回答。
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 75>>
      温特审视展板片刻，随后点了点头。
        “做得不错。结论是可靠的，只是论证中的几处环节太依赖推测。”
      参观者仍留在原地，继续查看你的复原图。
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 50>>
      “你找到了一个说得通的故事。”温特说道，
        “下次，在把它当成事实展示之前，先证明它。”
      <<He>>仍允许你的展览开放到下午。
    <<else>>
      参观者逐渐离开，温特则亲手修正了几张标签。
        “研究不是装饰。”<<he>>低声说道，“先拿出证据，再表现得胸有成竹。”
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br><<museumicon>><<lanLink 'Return to the museum' 'Museum'>><</lanLink>><br>

:: Museum Golden Priestess Statuette []
<<effects>><<museumClearHint 'antiquegoldpriestess'>><<npc Winter>><<person1>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Winter studies the statuette's kneeling robes and the script around its base through the glass.
    "A priestess making an offering," <<he>> says. "Not a soldier."
    <br><br>
    "Its recorded position matters more than the gold.
      Together with the script and the surviving accounts of the forest sanctuary,
      it identifies the ruin as an old temple tied to the same religious tradition.
      It does not tell us what sank it."
  <<option 'CN'>>
    温特隔着玻璃，仔细观察女祭司像跪伏的长袍与底座周围的文字。
    “正在奉上供物的女祭司。”<<he>>说道，“不是士兵。”
    <br><br>
    “它被发现的位置，比黄金本身更重要。
      结合上面的字形和现存的森林礼拜场所记录，
      它可以确认湖底废墟是一座古老神殿，与同一宗教传统相联。
      它却无法告诉我们，那座神殿为何沉没。”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<museumicon>><<lanLink 'Return to the museum' 'Museum'>><<endevent>><</lanLink>><br>
